 files."] [135 1 "// Len is the number of items."] [162 1 "// matches is whether entry i's key (of the hash looked up) is key: the same object, the same str, else __eq__."] [182 3 "// directly, not through the slot: the types' dictionaries are filled by init functions that may"] [183 3 "// run before str's sets its slots"] [193 1 "// Get is d[key], nil when absent."] [206 1 "// Set is d[key] = v."] [231 1 "// insertNew appends key (of hash h, not in the dict) with value v."] [257 1 "// Delete removes key; false when absent."] [267 50 "// a hole; its chain link kept"] [276 1 "// Clear empties the dict."] [285 1 "// GetStr and SetStr are Get and Set with a str key (the namespaces')."] [293 1 "// nameStr is the interned str of a name GetStr and SetStr look up (attribute and special names), a code's co_names"] [294 1 "// or an identifier-like str constant, so each is made and hashed once: sys.intern's table (internTable), as CPython"] [295 1 "// interns them all in one (queue 211; before it a table of its own, so `sys.intern(s) is name` could fail). At most"] [296 1 "// nameStrsMax names are added to it this way."] [313 1 "// Items calls f on each item in order until it returns false."] [323 1 "// Keys is the keys in order."] [330 1 "// Copy is a shallow copy."] [344 1 "// Update is dict.update(o): a mapping's items (keys() and []), or an iterable of pairs."] [347 3 "// the other dict's entries by position, its change by a key's __eq__ an error (dict_merge's check of"] [348 3 "// dk_nentries; queue 203: test_merge_and_mutate)"] [378 3 "// PySequence_Fast(x, \"object is not iterable\"), its TypeError given the note (dict_merge_from_seq2; queue 203:"] [379 3 "// test_update_type_error)"] [414 16 "// a reverse iterator: i counts the entries left, from the last"] [415 16 "// the items still expected (di->len)"] [416 16 "// the dict's compactions when made"] [457 1 "// dictNew is dict(), dict(mapping or iterable, **kwargs)."] [588 4 "// the size checked, the iteration ended past the entries of a dict refilled since, and the keys changed"] [589 4 "// when it meets an item it did not expect (dictiter_iternextkey_lock_held, dictreviter_iter_lock_held;"] [590 4 "// queue 203: test_reversed_dict_after_clear_and_restore; before it any change of the keys was one)"] [595 4 "// compacted since (CPython's resize, at other moments): the positions lost, the keys changed"] [627 3 "// __reduce__ is dictiter_reduce: (iter, (list,)), the list the items a copy of the iterator would give,"] [628 3 "// the iterator itself not advanced (queue 211: test_dict's six *iterator_pickling tests)"] [671 2 "// a view's mapping: a mappingproxy of its dict (dictview_mapping; queue 203: test_views_mapping)"] [703 1 "// dictViewCompare is dictview_richcompare: the sizes, then every item of one in the other by the other's"] [704 1 "// containment (an items view's: the key looked up, the values compared), no set made (queue 203: an unhashable"] [705 1 "// value compared, test_errors_in_view_containment_check)."] [787 1 "// dictMissing is d[k] on a dict subclass with __missing__: the method called with the key."] [803 1 "// newDictSubclass makes an instance of a dict subclass; PY5c sets it (by default the base value: PY5c wraps it)."] [840 3 "// the key hashed and looked up once (dict_setdefault_ref; queue 203: test_setdefault_atomic)"] [886 5 "// the slot leaves the index too: a later key of its hash looked up entries[i] past the end"] [887 5 "// (PY6e's REQUEST: test_os's mapping tests popitem then set)"] [888 5 "// the popped entry and the holes after it leave the index too: a later key appended at their"] [889 5 "// positions is found by its own chain only"] [926 2 "// dict.fromkeys, a class method (dict_fromkeys: cls() filled by its __setitem__; PY7: it was a plain built-in,"] [927 2 "// bound to an instance, d.fromkeys(keys) iterated d)"]] :go/pos {:name [1 9] :package [1 1]} :go/semis [[102 28] [126 25] [146 17] [146 47] [153 35] [168 22] [169 25] [181 24] [302 31